anv/nvmtl: GPU reset recovery - replace a banned exec queue on the same VM

nvmtl_anv_device_recover_v1(VkDevice, flags, info), looked up with dlsym by the nullmoth Metal plugin: each banned exec
queue (and companion RCS queue) of the device is replaced by a fresh one on device->vm_id, the new context gets anv's
initial queue state again (genX(init_queue_state), split out of genX(init_device_state)), the old queues are destroyed
and the queue and device lost flags are cleared. This is what Linux userspace does after an xe context ban (iris replaces
its exec queue); the VM, BOs and GPU addresses survive, so every Vulkan handle the plugin holds stays valid. flags:
FORCE (replace every queue, waiting for it to go idle: tests), QUERY (report only). The caller serializes submissions
and fence waits around it. Base: Mesa "tile4v" = tile4 + 0040-0043 (51b37d76, mesa-wsi build-cpu3); touches no file of 0040-0043.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

